{{!-- Shelf price: the item's price AFTER the merchant's modifier. The system's own price
      column reads system.price.value straight off the item and knows nothing about the
      markup, so it would quote a number the buyer is never charged.

      The class must be item-<columnId>: dnd5e sizes columns with CSS keyed on that class
      for BOTH the header cell and the row cell, so any other name leaves the two out of
      step. Widths for these three live in styles/lootshelf.css. --}}
<div class="item-detail item-shelfPrice {{#unless ctx.shelf.priceLabel}}empty{{/unless}}"
     data-column-id="shelfPrice">
    {{#if ctx.shelf.priceLabel}}{{ ctx.shelf.priceLabel }}{{/if}}
</div>
